{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Petrified Legions triggers Call of the Darkwing from physical damage (#1839)",
  "contract": "Petrified Legions 500012's single effect is SPELL_AURA_PROC_TRIGGER_SPELL (aura 42) on Call of the Darkwing 801958, a native SPELL_EFFECT_SUMMON with MiscValue 50069 (Shadow Bat), MiscValueB 61 and DieSides 2. Spell.dbc gives 500012 ProcFlags 0 and no spell_proc row existed, so the aura was inert. The tooltip is 'Physical damage you deal or take now has a $h% chance to trigger a Call of the Darkwing' and the record's own ProcChance is 10, which this scenario does not change. Bloodfang Bite rank 572551 is SchoolMask 1 (Physical) and DmgClass 2, matching the row's SchoolMask 1 and its melee-damage-class bits; it needs a Cursed Form for its CasterAuraSpell 525031, supplied by Eternal Curse through the module's marker sync. Each bite costs 300 rage units (30 Rage), so Rage is restored before every bite; a single 1000-unit fixture pays for only three and the rest fail with SPELL_FAILED_NO_POWER. The proc is counted with spell_proc_count, which records every Call of the Darkwing cast with Petrified Legions as its triggering aura, rather than with living Shadow Bats: the bats live 15 s (DurationIndex 8), so a bat count only sees the last 15 s of events, and whether the summoned bat appears is Call of the Darkwing's own behavior, covered by bloodmage-screech-of-the-darkwing. 66 connecting bites at 10% leave 0.9^66, about 0.096%, chance that a correctly fixed build records no proc; the melee auto attacks in both directions add further physical events and only lower it. A build without the spell_proc row records zero every time.",
